        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0183" n="176" xml:id="pg176"/>

                <head>No. 102.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Braida to Mr. Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >San Juan del Norte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 25, 1894.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to transmit herewith a letter just
                    received from Capt. B. B. Seat, United States consular agent at Bluefields,
                    addressed to me, in order to contradict false representations, most inopportune
                    at the present moment and injurious to our citizens. I also include copy of a
                    report of Mr. Seat to Capt. Commander G. W. Sumner, of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi>, dated August 15.</p>
                <p>Her Britannic Majesty’s ship <hi rendition="#italic">Mohawk</hi> arrived off Grey
                    Town this morning, coming from Port Limon. Mr. H. F. Bingham, the former consul,
                    came ashore, when the man-of-war left in the direction of Blue-fields, 10
                    a.m.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. C. Braida.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d102-a1.xml" xpointer="d102-a1"/>
